[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $h,\gamma,\lambda>0$ and  $T>0$ such that $n\coloneqq T/h\in\mathbb{N}$. Assume that there is a recurrence relation of the form 
    \begin{align*}
        f_{j+1}\le \bigl(1+ h\gamma \bigr)f_j+\lambda \qquad j=0,\dots,Tn-1
    \end{align*}
    such that $f_0=0$. Then it follows that
    \begin{align*}
        f_j\le \lambda \sum_{k=1}^j (1+h \gamma )^{k-1} .
    \end{align*}
    In particular $f_j\le \frac\lambda{h\gamma}  e^{T\gamma}$.

