body:
[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] The cumulants have the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $k_n(cf)=c^nk_n(f)$.

\item $k_1(f+d)=k_1(f)+d$, and $k_n(f+d)=k_n(f)$ for $n>1$.

\item $k_n(f+g)=k_n(f)+k_n(g)$, if $f,g$ are independent.
\end{enumerate}

