body:
[Corollary cor:exp_mom_local_time of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] For any sequence $s_n \to s>0$, any $C>0$ and uniformly for all $x \in [-C\sqrt{n}, C\sqrt{n}]$, there is a constant $K>0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \limsup_{n \to \infty}\Exp{\exp\left(s_n\frac{Y_n(C,x)}{\sqrt{n}}\right)}\leq K <\infty.
    \end{align*}

