[Theorem 19 (Intersection of cells at small intensitites) of arXiv:2504.02435, 'Poisson-Voronoi percolation in higher rank'] Let $G$ be a connected higher rank semisimple real Lie group and $(X,d_X)$ be its symmetric space.
    Then for every $\eps>0$ and $R>0$ there is $\lambda_0\in (0,1]$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}^{(\lambda)}\left(\forall i,j \in \mathbb{N} \  \left[C^{(\lambda)}_i\cap \mathcal{B}_R(o)\not=\emptyset\not= C^{(\lambda)}_j\cap \mathcal{B}_R(o) \  \Rightarrow \  C^{(\lambda)}_i\cap C^{(\lambda)}_j\not=\emptyset \right]\right)>1-\eps
    \end{equation}
    for every $0<\lambda\le \lambda_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem d4 of arXiv:2606.16237, 'The Backward Stochastic Partial Differential Integral Equations: Solvability and Compariso'] Assume that the conditions of Theorem (thm:b2 of the paper) hold. If \((u, q, r) \in \mathbb{S}^2(H^1) \cap \mathbb{H}^2 \times \mathbb{H}^1\times \mathbb{H}^{\nu,1}\) is a strong solution of BSPDIE (equation eq:3.2 of the paper), then there exists a constant \(C > 0\) depending  on \(\alpha\), \(K\), \(\kappa\), \(T\), and the function \(\gamma\) in Assumption (ass:b3 of the paper), such that
\begin{equation}
E\left[\sup_{0 \leq t \leq T} \| u(t) \|_1^2 \right] + ||| u |||_2^2 + ||| q |||_1^2 + ||| r |||_{\nu,1}^2
\leq C \left( ||| f_0 |||_0^2 + E\|\varphi\|_1^2 \right).
\end{equation}

