body:
[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] We have $\bbP$-almost surely that for $r\in [0,1]$,
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{f_t(rJ_{ij},J_{i,-j})}{f_t(\bfJ_i)}=\exp\bigg(\frac{\beta(r-1)}{\sqrt N}J_{ij}\int_0^tX_s^j dB_s^i-\frac{\beta^2(1-r)^2}{2N}|J_{ij}|^2\int_0^t |X_t^j|^2\,ds\bigg).
    \end{align*}
    In particular there exist constants $C_{\fru},C \in (0, \infty)$ that depend only on $(\beta,T,A,\sigma^2)$ such that if  $\sqrt N > C_{\fru}$, for all $r$ we have
    \begin{align*}
        \bbE_\bbP\bigg[\Big| 
        \frac{f_t(rJ_{ij},J_{i,-j})}{f_t(\bfJ_i)}\Big|^8\bigg]\leq C
    \end{align*}

