[Define Definition 4.1 of arXiv:2601.09990, 'Remarks on the convex integration technique applied to singular stochastic partial differe'] Given initial data $u^{\text{in}} \in L^{n} (\mathbb{T}^{d})$, a scalar field $u \in L^{n} (0, \infty; L^{n} (\mathbb{T}^{d}))$ is a weak solution to (equation odd power of the paper) if 
\begin{align}
&\int_{\mathbb{T}^{d}} u(t,x) \psi(t,x) dx - \int_{\mathbb{T}^{d}} u^{\text{in}} (x) \psi(0,x) dx - \int_{0}^{t} \int_{\mathbb{T}^{d}} u(s,x) \partial_{s} \psi(s,x) dx ds  \nonumber \\
& \hspace{30mm} + \int_{0}^{t} \int_{\mathbb{T}^{d}} u^{n}(s,x) \psi(s,x) dx ds = \int_{0}^{t} \int_{\mathbb{T}^{d}} u(s,x) \Delta \psi(s,x) dx ds 
\end{align} 
for all test function $\psi$ in $C_{c}^{\infty} ( (-\infty, T) \times \mathbb{T}^{d})$.

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:919f214b96c7b94837146a6d0d138438d6858b69c9993be8ae4acad2c81d4f2f","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/91/919f214b96c7b94837146a6d0d138438d6858b69c9993be8ae4acad2c81d4f2f.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:d6e4f92136ac5073572898d3e60154ba2623e292172e163f39dac38e7c6984db","bundle_entry_key":"2609-02398-lemma-2-half","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_150","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_150.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-02398-lem-2-half","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Fix $X \in \SE(\sigma^2,\alpha)$ and $t < 0$. Since $(x - t)_+ = (x - t) + (t - x)_+$ and $\E[X] = 0$,
\begin{align}
    S_X(t) = \E[X - t] + \E[(t - X)_+] = -t + \E\left[\left((-X) - (-t)\right)_+\right] = -t + S_{-X}(-t).

\end{align}
The class is closed under sign flip, so $-X \in \SE(\sigma^2,\alpha)$, and $-t > 0$, whence $S_{-X}(-t) \le S_{c\Lap}(-t)$ by hypothesis. Applying \eqref{eqn:flip} to $c\Lap$ and using $-c\Lap \overset{d}{=} c\Lap$,
\begin{align*}
    S_{c\Lap}(t) = -t + S_{-c\Lap}(-t) = -t + S_{c\Lap}(-t).
\end{align*}
