[Proposition 30 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] For any bounded cylindrically Lipschitz function $h\in C_{b,Lip}(\mathbb{R}^n)$ and arbitrary $s\geq 0$, there holds
         \begin{equation*}
             \lim\limits_{t\rightarrow0} \mu_{n,s+t}h=\mu_{n,s}h.
         \end{equation*}

[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2606.30411, 'Notes on constants for maxima of Rademacher averages'] Let \(G_1,\ldots,G_p\) ($p\in\Nb$) be independent standard normal random variables. Then
\begin{equation*}
    \inf_{p\geq 1}\frac{\Eb \max_{1\leq j\leq p}|G_j|}{\sqrt{\log(2p)}} = \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi\log 2}}.
\end{equation*}

