[Lemma of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Given any $r_1, \ldots, r_k \in \alpha \times \alpha$, set $\gamma \coloneqq {\textsc{Supp}}(r_1, \ldots, r_k)$. Then for any $\beta \subseteq \alpha$ and all $\mathbf{t}$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
         \Phi_{\beta}^{(r_1, \ldots, r_k)}(\mathbf{t}) =  \Phi_{\beta \cap \gamma}^{(r_1, \ldots, r_k)}(\mathbf{t}).
    \end{align*}

