[Lem l-v-lemma of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] For $V$ as in (equation def-of-V-for-SPDE of the paper) we have $V \in \tilde{\mathcal{D}}^{ext}_+(\mathcal{M}_+)$ (see (spde-tilde-domain of the paper)) and
    \begin{equation*}
    \begin{aligned}
        \mathcal{L} V(r,v,z) &= h'(r)r\Big[\ip{v}{\tilde e_u} + \ip{\tilde F_u(r,v,z)}{1_u}\Big] + \frac{1}{2}h''(r)r^2\|\tilde G_u(r,v,z)^*1_u\|_U^2 \\
        \Gamma V(r,v,z) &= h'(r)^2r^2\|\tilde G_u(r,v,z)^*1_u\|_U^2 \,,
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
where the adjoint of $G_u(r,v,z)$ is taken in $\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{U},L^2)$ and $\tilde e$ is as in (def:tilde-e of the paper).

[Definition of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Consider a matrix $X\in M^{n\times m}(\mathbb{C})$ with all i.i.d.\ complex Gaussian entries such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{E} X_{j,k}=\mathbb{E}X_{j,k}^2=0,~\mathbb{E}|X_{j,k}|^2=1
    \end{equation*}
    for any $j,~k$. Then the Hermitian matrix $W_{n,m}:=X^*X\in M^{m}(\mathbb{C})$ is called a \textbf{complex Wishart matrix}, or a \textbf{Laguerre Ensemble}.

[Corollary cor.expansion_trunc of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For any $\delta \in [0, 1-\mathfrak{p}]$, the conductivity perturbation $\widetilde\Delta^{\delta}_m$ defined in (equation eq.defDeltaTrunc of the paper) satisfies 
			\begin{equation}
				\mathbb{E} [\widetilde\Delta^{\delta}_m] = \sum_{l=0}^{\vert E_d({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m) \vert} \widetilde c_{l,m} \left(\frac{\delta}{1-\mathfrak{p}}\right)^l,
			\end{equation}
			with the coefficient $\widetilde c_{l,m} $  defined as 
			\begin{equation}
				\widetilde c_{l,m} := \frac{1}{|{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m|}\sum_{e\in E_d({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m)}\mathbb{E}
				\left \langle \nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}),(\mathbf{a}^e-\mathbf{a})\sum_{\substack{G \subseteq E_d({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m) \\ |G|=l-1}}D_{G}\big(\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}^e)\big)\right \rangle_{{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m}.
			\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 17 (Doob's optional stopping version II, general supermartingale) of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] Let $\{f_j\}_{j \geq 0}$ be a given  real-valued supermartingale on $\mathcal{S}$. Consider two stopping times satisfying  
$\rho\le \tau$ a.e. and assume that $(L)-a.e$ holds. Then, if $\tau \leq C ~~a.e.$, where $C$ is a non negative integer:
\begin{equation}
\overline{\sigma}_{\rho} f_{\tau} \leq f_{\rho}\;\;\mbox{a.e. on}~~\mathcal{S}.
\end{equation}

