[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Let $v_1^\e$ be defined by \eqref{e2-7}. Then,
\begin{equation}
\lambda v_1^\e(x)-\sL_\e v_1^\e(x)= G_1^\e\left(x,\e^{-1} x \right)+\bar F_1^\e(x),
\end{equation}
where $G_1^\e:\R^d\times \T^d \to \R$, $F_1^\e:\R^d\times \T^d\to \R$ and $\bar F_1^\e:\R^d \to \R$ are defined respectively by
\eqref{l2-2-2} and \eqref{l2-1-3}.

[Definition 3 of arXiv:2609.00702, 'On the Set-Valued Katugampola Fractional Integral: Properties and Regular Selections'] Let $F:I\rightrightarrows \mathbb{R}$ be a set-valued function and $\mathfrak{I}$ be the collection of all integrable selections of $F.$ Riemann-Liouville set-valued fractional integral of $F$ is defined as 
    \begin{equation*}
        \begin{aligned}
            _a\mathfrak{D}^{\nu}F(t)=\bigg\{\frac{1}{\Gamma(\nu)}\int_a^t(t-x)^{\nu-1}f(x)dx:f\in\mathfrak{I}\bigg\}
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation*}
    where $\nu>0$ is a real number.

[Theorem 15 (Strict endpoint chain for $1\le p<2$) of arXiv:2605.11451, '2605.11451'] For every $1\le p<2$ and every $k\ge1$,
\begin{equation}
 b_{p,k+1}<b_{p,k}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every $n\ge2$,
\begin{equation}
 A_{p,n,0}(u^{(1)})>
 A_{p,n,0}(u^{(2)})>
 \cdots>
 A_{p,n,0}(u^{(n)}).
\end{equation}

