[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $T = \E X >0,$ and assume that $X \sim f \dd \pi_{T}.$ If $f$ is bounded away from zero and infinity, then
    \begin{displaymath}
        \limsup_{n \rightarrow \infty} \Bigg[ n^{2}  H \Big( \sum_{i=1}^{n} T_{1/n}(X_{i}) |\pi_{T} \Big)  \Bigg] \le  \Big( \frac{\Var(X)}{T } - 1 \Big)^{2}.
    \end{displaymath}

