[Lemma lem:mult_concentration of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Let $k_i$ denote the number of tiles on edges of type $e_i$, and let $\overline{k}_i = \mathbb{E}_{\mu_{n,N,w}}[k_i]$. There exists a constant $c=c(w)>0$ such that for any $\varepsilon>0$ and $N$ large enough given $n,\varepsilon$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}_{\mu_{n,N,w}}(|k_i-\overline{k}_i|>\varepsilon \overline{k}_i)\leq \exp(-\varepsilon^2 N/2cn^d).
    \end{equation}

