body:
[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2608.31145, 'Gauge-compatible tensors on statistical manifolds: splitting and submanifold geometry'] Let $M$ be a $\Theta$-CR submanifold of a $\Theta$-statistical
manifold.

\begin{enumerate}
\item For $X,Y\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta})$,
\begin{equation}
F_{\Theta}([X,Y])
=
h(X,\Theta Y)-h(Y,\Theta X).
\end{equation}

\item For $U,V\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta}^{\perp})$,
\begin{equation}
P_{\Theta}([U,V])
=
A_{\Theta U}V-A_{\Theta V}U.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}

Consequently:

\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] if
\[
\ker(F_{\Theta}|_{TM})=D_{\Theta},
\]
then $D_{\Theta}$ is integrable if and only if
\begin{equation}
h(X,\Theta Y)=h(Y,\Theta X)
\end{equation}
for all $X,Y\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta})$;

\item[(b)] if
\[
\ker(P_{\Theta}|_{TM})=D_{\Theta}^{\perp},
\]
then $D_{\Theta}^{\perp}$ is integrable if and only if
\begin{equation}
A_{\Theta U}V=A_{\Theta V}U
\end{equation}
for all $U,V\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta}^{\perp})$.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:aniso_inj_holder of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] For every $\alpha\in (0,1)$, any element $T\in \mathcal{C}^{\alpha,\alpha-1}_{x,y}(I\times J)$ for every $\chi\in C^\infty_c(J)$, the product $T1_I\chi$ which is well--defined
also belongs to the H\"older space $\mathcal{C}^{\alpha-1}(I\times J)$.     
\begin{comment}
In fact the above result also holds true for the product $T1_{I\times J}$ instead of $T1_I\chi$~: 
$T1_{I\times J}\in \mathcal{C}^{\alpha-1}(\mathbb{R}^2 )$ with support $I\times J$.    
\end{comment}

