body:
[Lemma lem:RGrowth of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] There exist some constant $C_0 > 0$, depending only on $C$, $d$, and $m$, such that for all $\delta \in (0, 1]$ and $n$ sufficiently large, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        R(\delta \left\lvert\mathrm{Centre}(C)\right\rvert) \leqslant C_0 \delta^{\alpha} \sqrt{n}, 
    \end{equation*}
    where $\alpha = (d-1)^{-1}(m-1)^{-1}$.

