[Proposition pro:approximation_CLT of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] For each exponent $\delta>0$, there exists $C:=C(d,\mathfrak{p},\delta)>0$ such that on the event $\{y\in\mathscr{C}_\infty\}$, when $t>\mathcal{T}_{par,\delta}(y)$, we have
		\begin{equation}
			\sup_{f\in 1\text{-}\mathrm{Lip}(\mathbb{R}^d)}\Bigg\vert \sum_{x: x + y\in\mathscr{C}_\infty}f(x)\left(p^\omega(t,x+y,y)-\theta(\mathfrak{p})^{-1}\bar{p}(t,x)\right)\Bigg\vert\leqslant Ct^\delta .
		\end{equation}
		Here $\mathcal{T}_{par,\delta}(y)$ comes from Lemma~(quantitative CLT of the paper).

