body:
[Corollary Cor:LIL_constant of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] Fix  $d\geqslant 2$ and $\mathfrak{p} \in (\mathfrak{p}_c(d), 1]$. For every $p \in [1,\infty)$, for almost every configuration $\omega\in\Omega$, and for all $y\in\mathscr{C}_\infty(\omega)$, the VSRW $(S_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ starting from $y$ satisfies the LIL
		\begin{align}
			P^\omega_y\Big(\limsup_{t\to\infty}\frac{|S_t|_p}{\sqrt{2t\log\log t}}= \gamma_{d,p} \bar{\sigma} \Big)=1,
		\end{align}
		and the CSRW $(\widetilde{S}_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ starting from $y$ satisfies the LIL
		\begin{align}
			P^\omega_y\Big(\limsup_{t\to\infty}\frac{|\widetilde{S_t}|_p}{\sqrt{2t\log\log t}}=\alpha_{d,\mathfrak{p}} \gamma_{d,p} \bar{\sigma}\Big)=1.
		\end{align}
		Here, $\bar{\sigma}$ is the diffusive constant in (equation equ:QIP of the paper), and constants $\gamma_{d,p}, \alpha_{d,\mathfrak{p}}$ are defined as
		\begin{align}
			\gamma_{d,p} := \max\left\{d^{\frac{1}{p}-\frac{1}{2}}, 1\right\}, \qquad \alpha_{d,\mathfrak{p}} := \big(2d\mathbb{E}_\mathfrak{p}[\omega\left(\{0,x\}\right)|0\in\mathscr{C}_\infty]\big)^{-\frac{1}{2}},
		\end{align}
		where $x$ is a neighboring vertex of $0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Openproblem 2 of arXiv:2606.11994, 'Sample Path Properties of the\\ Fractional Wiener--Weierstrass Bridge II'] In the critical case $H=K$, find a normalizing sequence $(a_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
 a_n\sum_{k=0}^{\floor{tb^n}-1}   |Y((k+1)b^{-n})-Y(kb^{-n})|^{1/H}

\end{equation*}
converges almost surely  to a finite limit for all $t\in[0,1]$. (Stated as a problem by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

