By definition of $k_0$ and Lemma (lemma: L_k asympto of the paper), we have $ m_{k_0} \ge c_\zeta (\log m)^\eta $. It follows from assumption (equation def: theta_eta of the paper) that $ \eta (2d\zeta - s) \zeta > 1 $. Therefore, the right hand side of (equation ineq: upper_bound_for _k_0 of the paper) goes to zero as $ m $","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:d9fc4246fa5eb2addc313034c57b6dc9f2b51671dbcdb6df5fd3d974caa130d1","revision_digest":"sha256:b01d1a3cf784f11347a0b830dc89aecdb10e9b4b1d1db7a096a53c30bc858cdb","source_id":"arxiv:2608.00399","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

