[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2506.11918, 'Central limit theorems for the Euler characteristic in the Random Connection Model for hig'] The variance $\V{\chi_a(\Delta_W)}$ is equal to
\begin{align*}
\sum_{k=1}^\infty \frac{\beta^k}{k!} \hspace{-2pt} \int_{W^k} \hspace{-4pt} \E{ \mathbb{E}\Big[ \Lambda_{(x_1,U_1),\dots,(x_k,U_k)}^{k} \chi_a(\Delta_W) \,\Big|\, \1\big\{ [x_1,\dots,x_k]\in\Delta_W^{x_1,\dots,x_k} \big\} \Big]^2 } \hspace{-1pt} \lambda^k (\d {(x_1,\dots,x_k})).
\end{align*}

