[Lemma lem:conv-fields-fractal of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D$ be a Jordan domain such that $\dim_M(\partial D)<2-1/4$. Let $\mathbb E_\delta$ denote the expectation under the (critical) coupling of Theorem (thm:master of the paper) in the discrete approximation $D_\delta$. For any continuous, bounded function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$ and any $n,k\geq1$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb E_{\delta}\big[(\tau_\delta, f)^n\ (\tau_\delta^\dagger, f)^k\big]\longrightarrow\mathcal{C}^{n+k}\ 2^{(n+k)/2}\ \mathbb E\big[(\field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)}, f)^n\ (\field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)}, f)^k\big]
    \end{equation}
    as $\delta\to0$. In particular, the fields converge jointly in distribution with respect to the (product) topology of the Sobolev space $H^{s}(\mathbb C)$ for any $s<-1$.

