[Lem lemma:decomposition of arXiv:2411.13926, 'Random walks on random walks:\\ non-perturbative results in high dimensions'] Let $B=\bigtimes_{x\in I} B_x$ be a cylinder event. 
Then, for any constraint set $\ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}$, it holds that $\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}_I(B \;|\; \ensuremath{\mathcal{C}})$ equals 
\begin{align}
&\prod_{x\in M^c} \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}_x(B_x) \sum_{y \in M} \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}_I(Y=y \;|\; \ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}) \prod_{x\in I_{>y}\cap M} \ensuremath{\mathbbm{1}}_{0\in B_x} \\
&\quad\cdot \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}_y(N_y \in B_y \;|\; N_y \geq 1) \ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}_{I_{<y}\cap M}( B_{I_{<y}\cap M} \;|\;\ensuremath{\mathcal{C}}^y).
\end{align}

