body:
[Lemma Corollary: Upper bound for cumulants of GUE of arXiv:2411.11341, 'Ultra high order cumulants and quantitative CLT for polynomials in Random Matrices'] Let $\mathcal{X}\sim GUE$. For any $r\geq 1$ and $m$ even,
\begin{equation}
|N^{r-2}K_r(\text{Tr}(Y_1),\dots,\text{Tr}(Y_r))|\leq|\mathcal{P}_2^i(m)| \prod_{k=1}^m ||D_{j_k}||,
\end{equation}
where
$$\mathcal{P}_2^i(m)=\{\tau\in \mathcal{P}_2(m): \tau\vee\gamma=1_m\text{ and }\tau\leq ker(i)\}.$$
In particular,
\begin{equation}
|N^{r-2}K_r(\text{Tr}(Y_1),\dots,\text{Tr}(Y_r))|\leq m!! \prod_{k=1}^m ||D_{j_k}||.
\end{equation}

