body:
[Theorem thm:char. unique ergodic of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Let $(\Omega,f)$ be a topological dynamical system, which is point transitive. Then the following two statements are equivalent:
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item the system $(\Omega,f)$ is uniquely ergodic;
			\medskip
			\item for any $X\in C(\Omega)$, we have $\overline{X}\in C(\Omega)$.
		\end{enumerate}

