body:
[Defn def:fsopwtp of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] Let $u$ be a non-negative, continuous, and $\mathscr{F}$-adapted,  $L^1(\mathbb T^d)$-valued process defined on $[0,T]$. For a point $x_0\in \mathbb T^d\setminus \mathrm{supp}(u_0)$ we define $R_0(x_0):= \mathrm{dist}_{\mathbb{T}^d}(x_0,\mathrm{supp}(u_0)) $. Then, for any $r\in (0,R_0]$, we say that $B_r(x_0)$ has \emph{waiting time $\tau_r(x_0)$}, where  
    \begin{equation}

        \tau_r(x_0) := \inf\left\{ t>0, \quad \int_0^t\int_{B_r(x_0)} u >0 \right\} \, \wedge\, T.
    \end{equation}

