[Proposition 6 (Negative drift of $X_n$) of arXiv:2607.20838, 'Long-memory Markov chains with power-law intensities'] Suppose that the model parameters satisfy 
	\begin{equation}
		\xi < \frac{p}{2 \gamma} 
	\end{equation}
	If $ c < 2 \gamma$, or equivalently $ c < p/\xi$,
	then there exists $x^* > 0$ such that for all $x > x^*$, the conditional drift of $X_n$ is negative, i.e.,
	$$\mathbb{E}_{x, c}[X_n] - x < 0.$$

