[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2607.22878, 'Clustering of large deviations in heavy-tailed moving averages: the catastrophe principle '] For $M, \delta>0$ and measurable sets $\Phi, \Psi \subset \RR^d \setminus B_{\delta}(0)$,
\begin{equation} 
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\sum_{i \neq j\in I_n^M } P\bigl( H_i^{(n)} Z_i
  \in \lambda_n \Phi, \, H_j^{(n)} Z_j \in \lambda_n \Phi)}{\sum_{i\in I_n^M } P(H_i^{(n)} Z_i \in \lambda_n \Psi)}=0. 
\end{equation}

