[Lemma cor:hill-2 of arXiv:2608.08375, 'Algebraic formulas for first-passage times of Markov processes in the linear framework: ge'] With the assumptions above, choose $z \in Z$. Let $W \subseteq \overline{Z} = \mathcal{V}(\mathcal{H}_u[G])$ be the vertex subset of $\mathcal{H}_u[G]$ given by $W = \mathcal{V}_{\text{out}}(u)$. Then,  
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{k \in W : k \to_G z}{\ell(k \to_G z) \, w(\Phi_{\{k\}}(\mathcal{H}_u[G]))}
    & = w(\Phi_{(Z \setminus \{z\}) \cup \{u\} \to Z}(G))\,, \\
    \sum_{z \in Z}{\sum_{k \in W : k \to_G z}{\ell(k \to_G z) \, w(\Phi_{\{k\}}(\mathcal{H}_u[G]))}}
    & = w(\Phi_Z(G))\,.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 82 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Suppose   that $(\sfd_{0},q,p)$ are properly tight.
 Then 
for any $\rho\leq \rho_{b} $, $\cF_{\tau}$-measurable $\bR^{d}$-valued $y$,  and Borel nonnegative $f$ 
given on $\bR^{d+1}$,
we have on $\{\tau<\infty\}$ that  
\begin{equation}

E_{\cF_{\tau}}\int_{0}^{\theta_{\tau}\tau_{\rho}(y) }f( t, x_{\tau+t} -y)\,dt\leq
N(d,\delta,p,q)\rho^{2}\dashnorm f\|_{L_{(q,p)}(C_{\rho})},
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}

E_{\cF_{\tau}}\int_{0}^{\theta_{\tau}\tau'_{\rho}(y)  }f( t, x_{\tau+t}-y)\,dt\leq
N(d,\delta,p,q)\rho^{2}
\sup_{C\in\bC_{\rho}}
 \dashnorm  
f\| _{L_{(q,p)}(C) }.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

