[Proposition 18 ({\cite{mingoFreeProbabilityRandom2017}}) of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] If $\{\mu_n\}_{n\in\mathbb N}$ is a sequence of probability measures on $\mathbb R$ such that
\begin{equation*}
G_{\mu_n}(z)\to G_\mu(z), \qquad z\in\mathbb C^{+},
\end{equation*}
for some probability measure $\mu$ on $\mathbb R$, then $\mu_n$ converges weakly to $\mu$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Let $c>0$ be a scale parameter and denote by $Y_c(t)$, $t \geq 0$, and $Y_c^+(t)$, $t \geq 0$, respectively, the CTRW and the OCTRW defined as above, depending on $c>0$. Assume that $(S^c_{[cu]},T^c_{[cu]})$, $u\ge0$, converges to $(A(u), S(u))$, $u\ge0$, weakly in $D([0, +\infty), \mathbb{R}^{d+1})$ {as $c\to +\infty$}\footnote{Here, the notation $[cu]$ denotes the integer part of the real number $cu$.}, with $S$ being strictly increasing and unbounded. Then, as $c \to +\infty$,
		\begin{align}
			&( Y_c(t), T_c(t) ) \to (A(L(t)-), S(L(t)-))^+\\
			& ( Y_c^+(t), T_c^+(t) ) \to (A(L(t)), S(L(t)))
		\end{align}
		weakly in $D([0, +\infty), \mathbb{R}^{d+1})$ (endowed with the Skorokhod $J$ topology).

[Theorem th: a priori branched0 of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Assume that $\Upsilon_\tau$ is globally Lipschitz continuous for all $\tau\in{\mathcal T}^{\leq N}$. Then, for sufficiently small $\varepsilon:=T\wedge\mu$ and $Z$ any solution of (equation eq:davie of the paper), 
	\begin{align*}
		\| Z^{[N+1]} \|_{(N+1)\alpha, \mu} &\lesssim_{\alpha, \mathbb{X}, \sigma} \sum_{i=1}^N \|Z^{[i]}\|_{i\alpha,\mu} 
		 \le 2\sum_{\tau\in{\mathcal T}^{\le N}} |\tau| \,|\Upsilon_{\tau}(Z_0)| \, \|\mathbb{X}(\tau)\|_{|\tau|\alpha}\,.

	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 19 (Hard-Edge Limit) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] We have, almost surely,
\[
\lim_{N \to \infty}
\left(
\frac{1}{4N}
+ 
\sum_{j \in \mathbb{Z}} \frac{\gamma_j^{N}}{\mu_j^{N} - z}
- 
\frac{\Gamma_N}{z}
\right)
=
\sum_{j \in \mathbb{Z}} \frac{\gamma_j}{\mu_j - z}
- 
\frac{\chi_{\alpha}}{z},
\]
for all $z \in \mathbb{R} \setminus \{\mu_j\}_{j \in \mathbb{Z}}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:lack of detailed balance of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] Assume that $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$ is a chemical system with sources and sinks. Assume that the system $(\Omega , \mathcal R, \mathcal K ) =(\Omega, \mathcal R , \emptyset ,  \mathcal K, \emptyset ) $ without sources and sinks satisfies the detailed balance condition.  Let $\mathcal B_{\mathcal W_r} = \{ w_k \}_{k =1}^{|\mathcal W_r |} $ be a basis for the space of the cycles of $(\Omega , \mathcal R, \mathcal K )$ and let $\mathcal B_{ \mathcal W} =  \{ w_k \}_{k =1}^{|\mathcal W |} $ be a basis of the space of the cycles of  $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$. Assume that 
 \begin{equation} 
 |\mathcal W| >  |\mathcal W_r |. 
 \end{equation}
 Then for every $w \in \mathcal W$ such that $ \pi_{ \mathcal R } w \notin \mathcal W_r $, it holds that 
 \begin{equation} 
 \Delta (w)= (E- D)^T \mathbb S_r \pi_{\mathcal R }  w
 \end{equation}
where $E \in \mathbb R^M $ is a solution to \begin{equation} 
 S_\rho^T  E = \ln \left( \dfrac{ K_{ - \rho} }{ K_{  \rho } }  \right)  \ \forall \rho \in \{ 1, \dots, r \}   
\end{equation} 
and where $D \in \mathbb R^M $ is the vector 
\[
D(k)= \begin{cases} &\log \left( \frac{\alpha_k }{ \beta_k } \right), \quad k \in \{ 1, \dots, |\Omega_c | \}   \\
& 0, \quad   k \in \{|\Omega_c | +1 , \dots , M \}. 
\end{cases}
\]

