[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For all~$\lambda\ge0$,
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty} \wt P\biggl(\,\bigcup_{x\in \BbbL_n}\bigl\{h(x)\ge \wt m_n-\lambda\bigr\}\cap\wt\BB_{n, k}(x)^\cc\biggr) = 0,
\end{equation}
where for $\tilde\sigma:=\frac1{12}$, 
\begin{equation}

\wt \BB_{n,k}(x):=\Bigl\{\wt m_k+k^{\tilde\sigma}\le \wt m_n-h(z)\le \wt m_k+k^{1-\tilde\sigma}\Bigr\}
\end{equation}
with our convention $z:=\frakm^k(x)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $f$ be three times weakly differentiable with derivatives of polynomial growth. Let $\sigma$ and $\xi$ satisfy Assumption \ref{Aspt_new}. Let Assumption \ref{Ass:Half_Step} hold and let $\delta,h \in (0,1/2)$ such that $\frac Th \in \mathbb{N}$. Then there is a constant $C>0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
         \Bigl|\E\bigl[ f(Y_T)\bigr]-\E\bigl[f\bigl(\tiX_T^{h,(1),N,\delta}\bigr)\bigr]\Bigr|
        \lesssim 
        h + \delta^{1-}
        + \frac1{\sqrt{N}} \delta^{-1} 
        \exp\Bigl(\frac T2
        h^{-1} \log\bigl( C  \delta^{-1}h^{-1/2}\bigr)\Bigr).
    \end{align*}

