body:
[Prop 21 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] Let $0<\A{1}\leq \A{2}\ll 1$ be such that there exists $\omega\in \hspace{0.1cm} ]0,1[$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        N^{-\omega}\leq \pr{\alpha_1\alpha_2}^{1/2}.
    \end{equation}
    Let $p\in S(1,\A{1},\A{2})$. Then, as $N\to +\infty$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \norme{p_{N,\A{1},\A{2}}}\leq \sup_{\rho\in \mc{T}_{\A{1},\A{2}}}\bb{p(\rho)}+o(1).
    \end{equation*}
    In particular, there exists a constant $C>0$ independent of $N$, $\alpha_1$ and $\A{2}$ such that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \norme{p_{N,\A{1},\A{2}}}\leq C.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma untied-truncation-stability of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Let \(\bar\mu\) be the admissible slow trajectory in
Lemma (lemma:untied-global-slow-dynamics of the paper), and fix \(T>0\). Let \(C_*\) be the spectral constant in Lemma (lemma:spectral_bounds_untied of the paper) and set
$R:=C_*^2$. Then there exist constants
$R<s_-<s_+<\infty$, $\varepsilon_T>0$ and 
$C_T<\infty$ such that the following holds.

If \(\nu_0\in X_{s_-}^0\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
\|\nu_0-\bar\mu(0)\|_{s_-}\le\varepsilon_T,

\end{equation}
then the extended ODE
\begin{equation}
\frac{d\nu}{d\tau}=V_{\rm ext}(\nu),
\qquad
\nu(0)=\nu_0,

\end{equation}
has a unique solution on \([0,T]\), remains in $\mathcal U_s$, and satisfies
\begin{equation}
\sup_{0\le\tau\le T}\|\nu(\tau)-\bar\mu(\tau)\|_{s_+}\le C_T\|\nu_0-\bar\mu(0)\|_{s_-}.

\end{equation}

