[Lemma lem:typewise_mean_error of arXiv:2609.02491, 'Generalised Random Parking for Trapeziums on a Strip'] There exists a finite constant $C>0$ such that, for all $x>(3a-b)/2$,
\begin{equation}
\max_{s\in\{\mathcal{P},\mathcal{T}\}}|e_s(x)| \le C\mathcal R_1(x), \quad \text{where}\quad \mathcal R_1(x) \coloneqq
\begin{dcases}
    \mleft(\dfrac{2e}{x/a}\mright)^{x/a-3/2},
    &\text{if }a=b,\\
    \mleft(\dfrac{2e}{x/a}\mright)^{x/a-5/2},
    &\text{if }a>b.
\end{dcases}
\end{equation}

