body:
[Lemma lem:G of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] There exists $C>0$ satisfying, for all $1/2<\lambda<1$,
	$T\ge0$ and $N\in\mathbb{N}$,
	\begin{equation}
		\int_0^T g_{\lambda,N}(t)\,{\rm d} t
		\le
		C\set{
			N^{-1}
			+
			N^{2\lambda-5/2}\,T^{1/2}
		}\; \text{.}
	\end{equation}

