[Proposition 68 of arXiv:2602.14618, 'Finitary coding and Gaussian concentration\\ for random fields'] Let $Y = (Y_n)_{n \in \Z}$ be a renewal process with $\gcd\{k\ge1:f_k>0\}=1$ (non-lattice inter-arrival distribution). The following are pairwise equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\arabic*)]
\item $Y$ satisfies a Gaussian concentration bound;
\item $\sum_{k\ge1}s^kf_k<\infty$ for some $s>1$;
\item $Y$ is a finitary process with exponential tail coding radius; 
\item $Y$ is a finitary coding of an i.i.d. process.
\end{enumerate}

[Proposition Matrix Bennett-Bernstein inequality \eqref{eqn:mbi} of arXiv:2411.09516, 'Sharp Matrix Empirical Bernstein Inequalities\footnote{NeurIPS 2025 Poster}'] Let $\overline \mathbf{X} _n$ be the sample average of independent $d\times d$ symmetric matrices $ \mathbf{X} _1,\dots,  \mathbf{X} _n$ with common mean $ \mathbb E   \mathbf{X} _i =  \mathbf{M} $, common eigenvalue upper bound $\lambda_{\max}( \mathbf{X} _i) \leqslant B$, and $ \sum_{i=1}^n \mathbb E   \mathbf{X} _i^2 \preceq n  \mathbf{V} $. For any $\alpha > 0$
\begin{equation}
     \mathbb P \left( \lambda_{\max} \left( \overline \mathbf{X} _n - \mathbf{M}  \right) \geqslant \frac{ B \log(d/\alpha)   }{3n} + \sqrt{  \frac{2 \log(d/\alpha) \| \mathbf{V} \|  }{n}}  \right) \leqslant \alpha.
\end{equation}

