[Lemma 10 (Hoeffding's Inequality) of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] Let ${\mbf{z}_{1}, \mbf{z}_{2}, \ldots, \mbf{z}_{N}}$ be independent random variables such that for each $i$, $z_i \in [a,b]$ almost surely. Then for any $\varepsilon > 0$, we have
	\begin{align}
	\prob_{\mbf{z}}*{
		\abs*{ \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} z_i - \mathbb{E}[z_i] }
		\ge \varepsilon 
		}
	\leq 2 \exp\parens*{ - \frac{2N \varepsilon^2}{(b-a)^2}  }.
	\end{align}

