[Proposition prop:parity of arXiv:2609.02544, 'A finiteness theorem for geodesic Leech wheels'] A geodesic Leech labeling satisfies
\begin{equation}
  \nu_A+\nu_B+\nu_A(m-\nu_A)-\chi_A+\chi_B=\ceil{N/2}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $\chi_A$ and $\chi_B$ are even.

[Lem 20 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] One has 
\begin{align}
\underset{t\rightarrow\infty}{\overline{\lim}}\frac{1}{\beta(t)}\sup_{\rho\leqslant r}\log & \mathbb{E}_{\rho,\sigma}\big[e^{-(\beta(t)-\delta)J_{t}(L_{\beta(t)-\delta}^{t})};W^{t}([0,\beta(t)-\delta])\subseteq\Sigma_{r+\varepsilon}\big]\leqslant-\chi_{r+\varepsilon}.
\end{align}

