[Lemma lem:ExitCentre of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $k \geqslant 2$, and suppose that the chain starts from a configuration $\eta \in {\mathrm{Centre}((k-1)C)}$. Let $\tau_{{\mathrm{Centre}(kC)}^{\mathsf{c}}}$ be the time it takes to exit ${\mathrm{Centre}(kC)}$. Then there exist constants $c_1, C_1 > 0$, depending only on $d$ and $m$, such that for any fixed $C > 0$ and all $\varepsilon > 0$,
    \begin{align*}
        \max_{\eta \in {\mathrm{Centre}((k-1)C)}} \Ps{\eta}{\tau_{{\mathrm{Centre}(Ck)}^{\mathsf{c}}} \leqslant \varepsilon (C/k) n} \leqslant C_1 \Exp{-c_1 (kC) \varepsilon^{-1}},
    \end{align*}
    for all $n$ sufficiently large.

