body:
[Lemma of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] The process $(\widetilde{B}^{s,1}_t)_{t \in [s, 1]}$ has negatively correlated increments. Moreover, for any $S \in [s, 1]$, and any partition $D= \{t_i\}_{i=1}^n$ of $[s, S]$, the $n\times n$ matrix $(Q^D_{ij})_{i,j=1}^n$ with entries 
  \begin{equs}
      Q^D_{ij}= \mathbb{E} (\widetilde{B}^{s,1}_{t_{i-1}, t_i}\widetilde{B}^{s,1}_{t_{j-1}, t_j})
  \end{equs}
  is diagonally dominant.

