[Defn weak_sol of arXiv:2412.05950, 'Quantitative particle approximation of nonlinear stochastic Fokker-Planck equations with s'] A family of random functions $\left\{\rho_t(\omega): t \ge 0, \omega \in \Omega\right\}$ lying in $S_{\mathcal{F} ^B}^{\infty}\left([0, T] ; L^1 \cap L^q\left(\mathbb{T}^d\right)\right)$ is a solution to ((SPDE_Ito of the paper)) if $\rho_t$ satisfies the following stochastic integral equation for all $\phi \in C^2\left(\mathbb{T}^d\right)$,

\begin{align}
\left\langle \rho_t, \phi\right\rangle &= \left\langle \rho_0, \phi\right\rangle+ \int_0^t\left\langle \rho_s F(\cdot\,, K \ast \rho_s), \nabla \phi \right\rangle ds \nonumber \\
& \quad +\frac{1}{2} \int_0^t\left\langle \rho_s, \sum_{i,j=1}^d \partial_{ij}\phi \,   \sum_{k=1}^d (\nu_s^{ik} \, \nu_s^{jk}+ \sigma_s^{ik} \, \sigma_s^{jk}) \right\rangle \, ds \nonumber \\
&\quad +\int_0^t\left\langle \rho_s, \sum_{i=1}^d \partial_i \phi\,  \sum_{k=1}^{d} \sigma_s^{ik} \right\rangle \, d B_s^k.   
\end{align}

