[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.30089, 'On the Coefficients of Hurwitz-Type Matrix Polynomials'] The $q\times q$ matrix polynomial $\f_n$ in (\ref{hup01}) is called
a Hurwitz-type matrix polynomial  (HTM) if there exist two sequences of
positive definite matrices, $(\cc_{k})_{k=0}^{m-1}$ and $(\dd_{k})_{k=0}^{m-1}$ 
(resp.  $(\cc_{k})_{k=0}^m$ and $(\dd_{k})_{k=0}^{m-1}$) such that, for $n=2m$,

\begin{align}
 \frac{\g_n (z)}{\h_n(z)}=
 &\cfrac{I_q}{z\cc_{0}+\cfrac{I_q}{\dd_{0}
 +\cfrac{I_q}{\ddots 
 +\dd_{m-2}+
 \cfrac{I_q}{
+z\cc_{m-1}+\dd_{m-1}^{-1}}}}}, 
\end{align}
for all $z\in \C$ with $\det \h_n(z)\neq0$ and, for $n=2m+1$,
\begin{align}

\frac{\h_n (z)}{z \g_n(z)}=
&\cfrac{I_q}{z\cc_{0}+\cfrac{I_q}{\dd_{0}+\cfrac{I_q}{\ddots \,
 +z\cc_{m-1}+\cfrac{I_q}{\dd_{m-1}
+z^{-1}\cc_{m}^{-1} }}}} 
 \end{align}

 for all $z\in {\mathbb C} \setminus\{0\}$ with $\det \g_n(z)\neq0$.

[Corollary Effective Independence of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For indices $i,j$ with $|\lambda_i - \lambda_j| \geq N^{-2/3+\delta}$ for some $\delta > 0$:
\begin{equation}
\left|\mathbb{E}[f(X_i^{(\mathbf{q})})g(X_j^{(\mathbf{q})})] - \mathbb{E}[f(X_i^{(\mathbf{q})})]\mathbb{E}[g(X_j^{(\mathbf{q})})]\right| \leq \|f\|_{\text{Lip}}\|g\|_{\text{Lip}} N^{-\delta/2+\varepsilon}
\end{equation}
for any Lipschitz functions $f,g : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

