[Proposition Theorem:GeneratorSemigroup of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] If $\mu\in\mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R})$ and $h\in\mathcal{C}^{1}(\mathbb{R};\mathbb{R})$ is bounded, then  
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{\theta\to0^{+}} \frac{\langle P_{\theta}^{*}[\nu], h \rangle - \langle \mu, h \rangle}{\theta} = \int_{\mathbb{R}^2}\mathcal{L}_{\boxplus}^{*}[Dh](r)(\nu\otimes\nu)(\mathrm{d}r),
\end{equation*}
where $\nu:=P_{\theta}^{*}[\mu].$

