[Lemma WPD-NHS-AA of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $N \in \left\{ {0,1, \cdots ,10} \right\}$ and $t \in \mathop  \cap \limits_{j = 0}^{q} \left[ {0,{\mathfrak{t}_j}} \right] \cap \left[ {{t_k},{t_{k + 1}}} \right)$, there exists a real number $\alpha \in \left( {\frac{\beta }{{b}},\beta } \right)$ such that the backward flow ${{\tilde \Phi }_k}\left( {t,x} \right)$ and the Lagrangian flow ${{\tilde X}_t}$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {\nabla {{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right\|_N} + {\left\| {{{\left( {\nabla {{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right)}^{ - 1}}} \right\|_N}  \lesssim \lambda _q^N \lambda _{q + 1}^{ - \alpha }   ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {D{{\tilde X}_k}} \right\|_N} \lesssim  \max \left\{ {1,\lambda _q^N \lambda _{q + 1}^{ - \alpha }} \right\}  ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {{{\bar D}_{t,\Gamma }}\nabla {{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right\|_N} + {\left\| {{{\bar D}_{t,\Gamma }}{{\left( {\nabla {{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right)}^{ - 1}}} \right\|_N} \lesssim \delta _q^{\frac{1}{2}}\lambda _q^{N + 1}   ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {{\partial _{tt}}{{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right\|_N} \lesssim \delta _q^{\frac{1}{2}}\lambda _q^{N + 1}  ,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {{\partial _{tt}}{{\left( {\nabla {{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right)}^{ - 1}}} \right\|_N} \lesssim \delta _q^{\frac{1}{2}} \lambda _q^{N + 3}   ,
\end{equation}
where ${{\bar D}_{t,\Gamma }} \triangleq {\partial _t} + {{\bar v}_{q,\Gamma }} \cdot \nabla $ is the material derivative corresponding to ${{\bar v}_{q,\Gamma }}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

