    To verify the upper semicontinuity of $\mathcal{V}_p^+$, suppose that $(t_j, m_j)\to (t,m)$ in $[0,1)\times\mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R})$.
    Using the definition of $\mathcal{V}_p^+(t_j,m_j)$, we can inductively choose integers $n_j>n_{j-1}$ along with $(k^{n_j}, \bm{x}^{n_j}) \in \{0,1,\dots,n_j-1\} \times {\mathbb R}^{n_j}$ such that
