[Cor 22 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] For $n = 2k+1$ odd, a.s. $\psi_{n,A}$ is a generalized function with
compact support contained in $A$.
For $n=2k\geq 2$ even, $\psi_{n,A}$ on $D\setminus A$ (more precisely when tested against functions compactly supported on
$D\setminus A$) coincides with
\begin{equation}

(-1)^{k}\dfrac{(2k)!}{2^{k} k!}
\Big(\dfrac{1}{2\pi}\log\Big(
\dfrac{\CR(z,D)}{\CR(z,D\setminus A)}
\Big)\Big)^{k}.
\end{equation}

