[Definition def:QIBis of arXiv:2608.05262, 'The law of $(1+1)$D SOS with an area tilt in a wedge'] We denote by $\mathbb Q_{\mathfrak h}^I$ the probability measure induced by $\widecheck \mathbb Q_\mathfrak h$  on the collection of paths  $\Phi=\{\underline{\widetilde{\phi}}(i), |i| \le N\}$ through the transformation
\begin{equation}

\widetilde \phi_r(i):= \left\{\begin{array}{ll}
 \widecheck \phi_r^-(i), & i \in [-N,a_r^-+\Delta],\\
\widecheck \phi^-_r(a_r^-+\Delta)+\widecheck \phi^o_r(i)-\widecheck\phi^o_r(a_r^-+\Delta),  & i \in [a_r^-+\Delta,a_r^+-\Delta),\\
\widecheck \phi^+_r(i), &i \in [a_r^+ - \Delta,N].
\end{array}
\right.
\end{equation}

