[Proposition prop:free-Poisson-moments of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] The limiting measure $\mu_{c,\lambda,v}$ is the free compound-Poisson law with
rate $1/c$ and jump distribution $\operatorname{Law}(cR)$. For every $k\ge1$ it has the
finite moment
\begin{equation}
  M_k=\int t^k\,\mu_{c,\lambda,v}(\,\mathrm{d} t)
  =\sum_{\pi\in\mathrm{NC}(k)}c^{k-|\pi|}
  \prod_{V\in\pi}\mathbb{E} R^{|V|}.

\end{equation}
Equivalently, its free cumulants are
\begin{equation}
  \kappa_k=c^{k-1}\mathbb{E} R^k
  =c^{k-1}\exp\!\left(\frac{k(k-1)}2\lambda v\right).

\end{equation}

[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Assume that Assumption~\ref{ass:joint-minorization} holds and that the multiplicative drift condition \eqref{eq:regenerative-drift} is satisfied. Then there exists $\theta_1>0$ such that, for the split chain started from the atom,

\begin{equation*}
\Ee_{\mathfrak a}\left[\exp\{\theta_1(L_1+|Y_1|_1)\}\right]<\infty.
\end{equation*}

Consequently all polynomial moment assumptions imposed on $L_1$ and $Y_1$ in this paper are satisfied. If a transition reward $g$ satisfies

\begin{equation*}
|g(x,y,k)|\leq c_g(1+|k|_1)
\end{equation*}

for some finite constant $c_g$, then

\begin{equation*}
\Ee_{\mathfrak a}\left[\exp\{\theta_2 R_1^*(g)\}\right]<\infty
\end{equation*}

for some $\theta_2>0$. In particular, the reward moment assumptions used in the functional inverse theorem hold, and the one-cycle reward measures used in the regenerative lattice proof are exponentially summable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def: def of good external field configuration event for cle singularity of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Recall the definitions of  $\mathsf{a}_i(\tau),\mathsf{b}_i(\tau),\mathsf{c}_i(\tau), \mathsf{d}_i(\tau), \mathcal{F}_i(\tau)$ from Proposition~(prop: adding external field fluctuation of the paper). Recall that we have chosen $\kappa=10^{-5}.$ We define the event $\mathcal{A}_i\subset\mathbb{R}^{\Lambda_N}\otimes\{0,1\}^n$ to be the collection of pairs $(h,\tau)$ such that $$|\mathsf{a}_i(\tau)-\mathsf{b}_i(\tau)-\mathsf{c}_i(\tau)-\mathsf{d}_i(\tau)|\le ({\epsilon} M^{\frac{7}{8}})^{2.7}\mbox{  and  }|\mathsf{a}_i(\tau)|\le ({\epsilon} M^{\frac{7}{8}})^{0.9}$$ and let $\mathcal{A}=\cap_{i=1}^n\mathcal{A}_i$.  In addition, we define the following events \begin{equation*}
    \begin{aligned}
        \mathcal{B}&=\{(h,\tau):\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\frac{\mathsf{b}_i^2}{2}-\mathsf{b}_i)\ge c_7{\epsilon}^2M^{\frac{7}{4}}|\tau| +\sum_{i=1}^n\frac{{\mathbb{E}}\big(\mathsf{b}_i^2\mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}\big)}{4} \},\\
    \mathcal{A}^*&=\{(h,\tau):|\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\mathsf{a}_i^2-\mathsf{b}_i^2)|\le 1\},
    \\
    \mathcal{C}&=\{(h,\tau):|\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{c}_i|\le 1\},~~~~
    \mathcal{D}=\Big\{(h,\tau):|\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{d}_i|\le \sqrt{\iota^{-2\kappa}\cdot \sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_i^2}\Big\}.
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation*}

