[Prop pr:expansion_init of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For every $m \in \mathbb{N}_+$, the mapping $\mathfrak{p} \mapsto {\overbracket[1pt][-1pt]{\mathbf{a}}}_m(\mathfrak{p})$ is polynomial, and its $k$-th derivative ${\overbracket[1pt][-1pt]{\mathbf{a}}}^{(k)}_m$ has an explicit expression
		\begin{equation}

			\forall \mathfrak{p} \in (0,1), \qquad \xi \cdot {\overbracket[1pt][-1pt]{\mathbf{a}}}^{(k)}_m(\mathfrak{p}) \xi =  \frac{k!}{(1-\mathfrak{p})^k} \sum_{\substack{|F|=k\\ F\subseteq E_d({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m)}} \mathbb{E}_{\mathfrak{p}}\left[D_F \mathscr{E}_{m,\xi}(\mathbf{a}) \right].
		\end{equation}

