[Thm Thomeo of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] Equip $\pazocal{P}_{[a,b]}$ with the weak topology and $\pazocal{S}^{\mathrm{adm}}_{[a,b]}$ with the subspace topology inherited from the product topology on $\prod_{n = 0}^\infty [0, (b-a)^n/n!]$. Then the primitive sequence map $S$ is a homeomorphism between $\pazocal{P}_{[a,b]}$ and $\pazocal{S}^{\mathrm{adm}}_{[a,b]}$; in particular, for $\mu_k, \mu \in \pazocal{P}_{[a,b]}$ with $k \geq 1$, 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mu_k \rightsquigarrow \mu \quad \Longleftrightarrow \quad \varepsilon_n(\mu_k) \to \varepsilon_n(\mu), \quad n \geq 0.
    \end{equation*}

