body:
[Theorem thm:lowerboundpt of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Under the same assumptions as in (thm:flowpoincare of the paper), it holds that for any observation period $T > 0$, and the initial condition $x_0 \in \mathcal{F}^\perp$, 
\begin{align} 
    \frac{1}{T}\int_t^{t + T} \lVertP_s x_0\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^2 \,\mathrm{d} s \le e^{- 2\nu t} \lVertx_0\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^2\,,
\end{align}
with the convergence rate: 
\begin{equation} 
    \nu = \frac{\gamma}{\gamma^2 C_0(T) + C_1(T)}\,,
\end{equation}
where $C_0(T)$ and $C_1(T)$ are the flow Poincar\'e constants in (thm:flowpoincare of the paper). 
Moreover, the convergence rate estimate (equation eq:ratel2 of the paper) is maximized at 
\begin{align} 
    \gamma_{\rm max} = \sqrt{C_1(T)/C_0(T)} \quad \text{with rate}\quad \nu_{\max} = \frac{1}{2\sqrt{C_0(T) C_1(T)}}\,.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 11 (Simplex additivity for persistence) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $\phi: K \rightarrow M$ be an admissible triangulation. Let $f: M \rightarrow \RR_{\ge 0}$ be a probability density, $\filt$ be either the Vietoris-Rips or \v Cech complex, and $\rmax_n$ be a radius cutoff parameter. Then there exists a constant $c>0$ so that for all integers $1 \le k \le d$, $\alpha \in (1, \infty)$ and sufficiently large $n$,
    \begin{align} 
        \bigg| \overline{\Pi}_{k, \filt}(nf)(\alpha) - \sum_{\dim\sigma = d} \overline{\Pi}_{k, \filt}(nf|_{\phi(\sigma)})(\alpha) \bigg| \le c \cdot n^{k+1} \rmax_n^{dk+1} (1 + n \rmax_n^d),
    \end{align}
    Furthermore, the persistence functional satisfies the simplex additivity \eqref{eqn:simplex_additivity1} if 
    the radius cutoff satisfies $n \rmax^d_n = o(n^{1/(d^2+d+1)})$.

