body:
[Theorem thm:stat.dist.alpha=0 of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting and $Y=(N,\Lambda)$. Under Assumption (a:finitereset of the paper) holds and with $\alpha=0$, there exists an invariant measure $\Pi$ for $Y$, given by the following, for $\lambda \in ({\lambda^o}, A)$:

\begin{equation} 
    \begin{split}
      \Pi(0, d \lambda) &=\frac{K_0}{{\lambda^o}} \delta_{{\lambda^o}}(d\lambda)\\
      \Pi(1, d \lambda) &=\frac{K_0}{\lambda}\,dG_{\ell}(1, \lambda-{\lambda^o})\\
      \Pi(n, d \lambda) &=\frac{1}{\lambda}  d\overline G_{\ell}(n,\lambda)
    \end{split}

\end{equation}
    with $K_0=\sum_{n=1}^\infty\int_{[{\lambda^o},A)}\lambda \bar{G}_{\ell}(n, (A-\lambda) \textrm{-})\Pi(n-1,d\lambda)$ and
    where $\overline \Pi(n,d\lambda) := \lambda \Pi(n,d\lambda)$
    and $\overline G_{\ell}^\star(n,\cdot) :=G_{\ell}(n,\cdot) \star \overline \Pi(n-1,\cdot)$.

[Definition Horizontal perimeter of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] For a measurable set $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$, its \emph{horizontal perimeter} is defined by
\begin{align*}
    \operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)=\sup\left\{\int_{\Omega}\sum_{i=1}^{d} X_i \rho_i: \|\sum_{i=1}^d \rho^2_i\|_\infty\leqslant 1, \rho_i\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb G)\right\},
\end{align*}
where $\{X_1, \ldots, X_{d}\}$ is an orthonormal frame in $V_1$. A measurable set $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$ is called a \emph{Caccioppoli set} if $\operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)<\infty$.

[Deff 4 (Extended Carre du Champ operator) of arXiv:2604.20435, 'Stochastic Extinction with Relaxed Boundedness Conditions'] Let $A\subset M$ be an open invariant set. Define $\mathcal D^{ext}_2(A)$ be set of all continuous $f : A \to \R$ such that there exist continuous functions $\Lom f : A \to \R$ and $\Gamma f : A \to [0, \infty)$ such that $M^f_t(x)$ \begin{equation}
	M^f_t(x) := f(X^x_t) - f(x) - \int_0^t \Lom f(X^x_s) ds
\end{equation}
is a cadlag square integrable martingale and the stochastic process 
\begin{equation}
	(M^f_t(x))^2 - \int_0^t \Gamma f(X^x_s) ds
\end{equation}
is a martingale for
	all $x \in A$.

[Proposition p:easycheeger of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let $G=(V,\mathcal{E})$ be a finite graph respecting Convention (conv;simple of the paper) with $|V|=N$ and let $\mu_k$ be the $k$-th smallest eigenvalue of the normalized Laplacian ${\ensuremath{\mathcal L}} $, for $k=2,\ldots,N$.
Then,
\begin{equation}
    \mu_k \le 2 \, \varphi_k(G)\,.
\end{equation}

