[Lemma WPD-NHS-HUD-BB of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $N \in \left\{ {0,1, \cdots ,10} \right\} $ and $t \in \mathop  \cap \limits_{j = 0}^{q} \left[ {0,{\mathfrak{t}_j}} \right] \cap \left[ {{t_k},{t_{k + 1}}} \right)$, the stream function ${\mathfrak{S}_\xi }\left( \cdot \right)$ defined by (equation IUHYU-DJ of the paper) admits
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {{\mathfrak{S}_\xi }\left( {{\lambda _{q + 1}}{{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right)} \right\|_N} \lesssim \delta _q^{\frac{1}{2}} \lambda _{q + 1}^N  ,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
{\left\| {{{\bar D}_{t,\Gamma }}{\mathfrak{S}_\xi }\left( {{\lambda _{q + 1}}{{\tilde \Phi }_k}} \right)} \right\|_N} \lesssim  \delta _q^{\frac{1}{2}}\lambda _{q + 1}^{N + 1}  ,
\end{equation}
and
