[Proposition 31 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] Let $\Gamma_{\BD}$ be a non-nested CLE$_4$ in $\BD$. Let $\delta > 0$. Then for each $x, y, z \in {\BD}$ with $\lvert x - z\rvert \wedge \lvert y - z\rvert \ge \delta$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\BP\!\left\lbrack\SCB^{B_\varepsilon(z)}(\SCL(x); D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}) \cap \SCB^{B_\varepsilon(z)}(\SCL(y); D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}) = \emptyset\right\rbrack \le \varepsilon^{2 + o(1)} \quad \text{as } \varepsilon \to 0, 
	\end{equation}
	at a rate depending only on $\delta$, where $\SCB^{B_\varepsilon(z)}(\SCL; D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}) \defeq \SCB_{D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}(\SCL, B_\varepsilon(z))}(\SCL; D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD})$. The same is true with two deterministic and disjoint connected arcs of $\partial\BD$ in place of $\SCL(x)$ and $\SCL(y)$. (In this case, the rate of~\eqref{eq:hitting-two-metric-balls} depends only on the deterministic arcs and is uniform over all $z \in \BD$.) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

