[Lemma rhodotuLq-est of arXiv:2609.00627, 'Global well-posedness of radially symmetric strong solutions to two-dimensional compressib'] Assume that (equation TH1. 1-1 of the paper) holds. Then for any $q>2$, there exists a constant $C$ depending on $T, q, \mu, \beta, \gamma, \|\rho_0\|_{L^\infty}$,  $\|\boldsymbol{u}_0\|_{H^1}$, and $\|\nabla\boldsymbol{d}_0\|_{H^1}$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\int_{0}^{T}(\|G\|_{L^\infty}+\|\nabla G\|_{L^q}+\|\rho\dot{\boldsymbol{u}}\|_{L^q})^{1+\frac{1}{q}}dt+\int_{0}^{T}t(\|\nabla G\|_{L^q}^2+\|\dot{\boldsymbol{u}}\|_{H^1}^2)\leq C.
	\end{equation}

