[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.00945, 'Ising model and percolation: from hexagonal lattice to 3-12 lattice'] For a general polygon $(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N})$, the pure partition functions for multiple $\SLE_{\kappa}$ are defined as 
\begin{align*}
    \LZ_{\alpha}^{(\kappa)}(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N}):=\prod_{i=1}^{2N}|\varphi'(y_i)|^h\times \LZ_{\alpha}^{(\kappa)}(\varphi(y_1),\ldots,\varphi(y_{2N})), \qquad\text{for }\alpha\in\LP_N, 
\end{align*}
where $\varphi:\Omega\to \HH$ is a conformal mapping such that $\varphi(y_1)<\cdots<\varphi(y_{2N})$. By M\"obius covariance~\eqref{eqn::COV}, this definition is independent of the choice of $\varphi$.

