	\end{equation}
and let $\{S=U_0<U_1<\ldots<U_N=T\}$ (with $N\in\Nsf$) be a partition of interval $[S,T]$.

If $Y_0\not\in \mathrm{supp}(f)$, then we have $Y_t=Y_0$ for all $t\in \llbracket0, N\rrbracket$ so that we have $|Y_t-Y_0| = 0 < R$ for every $t\in \llbracket 0, N\rrbracket$. Suppose therefore that $Y_0\in \mathrm{supp}(f)$. We prove that the estimate $|Y_t - Y_0| < R$ holds for every $t\in \llbracket 0, N\rrbracket$ by induction. Clearly, the claim holds for $t=0$. Assume that $|Y_t-Y_0| < R$ ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:16b3bc82afbd5489ab2a194d429f2fd1747c88562185c972075cb1160165ff70","revision_digest":"sha256:d1cc118d1a1e4941e96701509904e75ff744ebacd4379a44759948fbdceeb1ea","source_id":"arxiv:2609.01190","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

