[Lemma lem:green-energy-strict-positive of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] Every nonzero $\nu\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
        I_D(\nu)>0.
\end{equation}

[Theorem thm:maint of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Assume that $X$ is a real or complex i.i.d. matrix satisfying Assumption~(ass:mainass of the paper) and that, for simplicity, its spectrum is simple (see Remark~(rem:nonsimpspec of the paper)). Let $\mathcal{O}_{ij}$ be the overlaps defined in (equation eq:defover of the paper). Then, with very high probability, for any small $\xi>0$, we have
\begin{equation}

\sup_{i,j\in [n]}\big(n|\sigma_i-\sigma_j|^2+1\big)\left[\frac{\big|\langle \boldsymbol{r}_i, \boldsymbol{r}_j\rangle\big|^2}{\lVert \boldsymbol{r}_i\rVert^2\lVert \boldsymbol{r}_j\rVert^2}+\frac{\big|\langle \boldsymbol{l}_i, \boldsymbol{l}_j\rangle\big|^2}{\lVert \boldsymbol{l}_i\rVert^2\lVert \boldsymbol{l}_j\rVert^2}\right]\le  n^\xi,
\end{equation}
In particular, by a Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, this implies
\begin{equation}

\sup_{i,j \in [n]}\big(n|\sigma_i-\sigma_j|^2+1\big)\frac{|\mathcal{O}_{ij}|}{\sqrt{\mathcal{O}_{ii}\mathcal{O}_{jj}}}\le n^\xi.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:m-SDE of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] The marginal process $m_t$ satisfies the following: 
    \begin{align}
         d m_t= \Big((\lambda_1-h_t)-(1-\frac1N)\frac1\beta \Big)m_t d t+\sqrt{\frac2{\beta N}(1-m_t^2)} d W_t\,,
    \end{align}
    where $h_t$ is the normalized energy, 
    \begin{align}
    h_t=\frac{2H(X_t)}N=\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N\lambda_i X_{i,t}^2\,.
    \end{align}

