[Defn 10 of arXiv:2604.12233, 'An upper bound on the smallest singular value of dense random combinatorial matrices'] For a random variable $X$ and $\varepsilon\ge 0$, the L\'evy concentration of $X$ of width $\varepsilon$ is 
    \begin{equation*}
        \Ls(X,\varepsilon)=\sup_{x\in \R} \P(|X-x|<\varepsilon).
    \end{equation*}

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2605.07184, 'Convergence of Stochastic Gradient Descent with mini-batching and infinite variance'] Under \Cref{assumption:learning-rate-rv-again}, 
  \begin{align*}
    \lim_{n\to\infty} \sum_{i=1}^N b_i\overline{F}_0(b_ic_N) = 1 \; .
  \end{align*}

