[Prop LCSN-to-LCS3 of arXiv:2601.00119, 'The largest common subtree of two random trees'] Let $\mathscr{T}$ and $\mathscr{T}'$ be two independent Brownian continuum random trees such that $(n^{-1/2}\cdot\tau_n,n^{-1/2}\cdot\tau_n') \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{\mathrm d}  (\frac{2}{\sigma}\cdot\mathscr{T}, \frac{2}{\sigma'}\cdot\mathscr{T}')$. Then, jointly with this convergence,
\[\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}\operatorname{LCS}_N(\tau_n,\tau_n') \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{\mathrm d} \operatorname{LCS}_3\big(\tfrac{2}{\sigma}\cdot \mathscr{T},\tfrac{2}{\sigma'}\cdot \mathscr{T}'\big)\] 
for any integer $N\geq 3$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

