\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] For any fixed $({\bf s}, {\bf t}) \in D_0$   the value of the integral in \eqref{def_F}   remains the same if the contour of integration is replaced by any good contour ${\mathcal C}$ that separates
${\bf s}$ and ${\bf t}$ and lies  in the strip  $-\alpha<\re(z)<\alpha$.
\item[(ii)] Given a fixed good contour  ${\mathcal C}$ that lies in the strip  $-\alpha<\re(z)<\alpha$, the integral
