body:
[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2512.02661, 'Worst-case mixing estimates for Brownian motion with semipermeable barriers'] There exist absolute constants $\delta_0, \gamma, c>0$ such that the following holds for $\delta \leq \delta_0$.
	Consider $x_0,y \in \cD(\delta/2)$ with $\Vert x-y \Vert\leq (4/5) r_\delta$ such that $x_0$ and $y$ lie on the same side of every barrier.
	Then, for $\varepsilon \leq  \gamma r_\delta$,
	\begin{align}
		\bbP\bigl(X_{ r_\delta^2} \in\sB(y,\varepsilon) \mid X_0 = x_0 \bigr) \geq c(\varepsilon/ r_\delta )^2.
	\end{align}

