body:
[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] There are a real-valued function $\Gamma\in C^\infty(X\setminus S)$, a function $h_S\in\mathcal K^*$, and a nonzero constant $c_0$ depending only on the dimension such that, in the distributional sense,
\begin{equation}
  L_\omega\Gamma=h_S-c_0\delta_S
\end{equation}
Moreover, in a tubular neighbourhood of $S$,
\begin{equation}
  \Gamma=\log d^2+B+\Psi,
\end{equation}
where $B\in C^\infty(S)$, extended smoothly to the neighbourhood, and
\begin{equation}
  |\nabla^j\Psi|\le C_jd^{1-j}
  \qquad(j\ge0).
\end{equation}

