\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
 \mathcal{L}_{\kappa_1}(\theta)&=E[\exp\{-\theta\sum_{i=0}^{N_t}\xi_i\}]=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}P(N_t=k)(E[\exp\{-\theta\xi\}])^k\\
 &=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\frac{(\lambda t)^k}{k!}e^{-\lambda t}(E[\exp\{-\theta\xi\}])^k=e^{-\lambda t+\lambda tE[e^{-\theta\xi}]}\\
 &=(g(E[e^{-\theta\xi}]))^t,
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
which satisfies (\ref{laplace_n}). Now, suppose (\ref{laplace_n}) holds for $n$. We need to prove it holds for $n+1$. Observe
