body:
[Lemma lem-exp-mon-D-x of arXiv:2504.20963, 'Exponential moments of truncated branching random walk martingales'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm-tail-D-x of the paper), there exists $\mkern 1mu\overline{\mkern-1mu \theta\mkern-1mu}\mkern 1mu>0$, such that for all  $n \in \mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$ and $x\ge 0$,
\begin{equation}

 \widehat{\mathbb{E}}^{*}_{x}[ e^{\mkern 1mu\overline{\mkern-1mu \theta\mkern-1mu}\mkern 1mu  D^{(x)}_{n}}  ] \leq 2 . 
\end{equation}
  As a consequence, we have 
     \begin{equation}
    \ln f_{n}(\theta, x) \leq  2 \theta R(x) e^{-x}  \text{ for any } \theta \in [0,\mkern 1mu\overline{\mkern-1mu \theta\mkern-1mu}\mkern 1mu], x \geq 0. 
     \end{equation}

