[Proposition 15 (Algebraic argument I, Step 1) of arXiv:2605.28677, 'Weak universality for stochastic reaction-diffusion models\\ with long-range correlated no'] Let $[\beta]\geq0$ and assume that for all populated $ \beta' \prec \beta$ 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\EE^{\frac{1}{p}} \left|
\pi^{(\n)}_{xy\, \beta'}
\right|^{ p} \lesssim \ve^{|\beta'|-\langle\beta'\rangle} |x-y|^{\langle \beta' \rangle - |\n|}\,.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Then for all \(\gamma\) populated and not purely polynomial, we have
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\EE^{\frac{1}{p}} \left|
(\Gamma_{xy})_{ \beta}^{\gamma}
\right|^{ p} \lesssim \ve^{|\beta|-\langle\beta\rangle-|\gamma|+\langle\gamma\rangle} |x-y|^{\langle\beta \rangle - \langle\gamma\rangle}\,,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
with the implicit understanding that the exponents on the right-hand side in
\eqref{est_Gamma} are non-negative, unless the left-hand side is zero.

