[Lemma lemma5.7 of arXiv:2411.02362, 'Limit theorems for random Dirichlet series: boundary case'] Fix any $\gamma>0$ and put $\mathfrak{s}_n:=\exp(-\exp(n^{1+\gamma}))$ for $n\ge 1 
$. Let $N_1$ and $N_2$ be functions which take positive integer values, may depend on $\gamma$ and satisfy
$N_1(s)\geq 2$ for small positive $s$, $\lim_{s\to 0+}(\log\log N_1(s)/\log 1/s)=0$, $\lim_{s\to 0+}(\log\log N_2(s)/\log 1/s)=1$ and $\lim_{s\to 0+}s\log N_2(s)=0$. Then
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}f(\mathfrak{s}_n) \sum_{k=2}^{N_1(\mathfrak{s}_n)}\frac{(\log k)^{-1/2}}{k^{1/2+\mathfrak{s}_n}}\widetilde{\eta}_{k,1}(\mathfrak{s}_n)=0\quad\text{\rm a.s.}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}f(\mathfrak{s}_n) \sum_{k\ge N_2(\mathfrak{s}_n)+1}\frac{(\log k)^{-1/2}}{k^{1/2+\mathfrak{s}_n}}\widetilde{\eta}_{k,1}(\mathfrak{s}_n)=0\quad\text{\rm a.s.}
\end{equation}

