[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2608.21905, '\bf Ruin theory incorporating MIPP-type jumps'] For each integer $k\geq 1$ and for any $n\geq 2$ 
\begin{equation}
P(V^{(n)}_{J_1^{(n)}}=k)=\frac{P(V_1^{(n-1)}=k)}{P(V_1^{(n-1)}\geq 1)},
\end{equation}
where $J_1^{(n)}$ is the first jump time of $V_t^{(n)}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:minimum-local-dimension of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. Then, almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\),
\begin{equation}
\alpha_{\min}(\mu_\circ)=A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W).
\end{equation}

