body:
[Theorem thm1 of arXiv:2411.09716, 'Stable Tables'] The probability $f(n)$ that a given person is unmatched at a table with $n$ people is
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{1}{9} + \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^n\left(\frac{2n}{3} - \frac{8}{9} + \frac{2}{n}\right)
    \end{equation}
    when $n$ is odd, and
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{1}{9} - \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^n\left(\frac{2n}{3} - \frac{8}{9}\right)
    \end{equation}
    when $n$ is even. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

