[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] Suppose the process $\mathbf{X}=\{X_n:n\geq0\}$ is defined by \eqref{111} and satisfies {\bf (B)}. Then as $n\to \infty$,  
\begin{align*}
\frac{S_n-\beta K_n/(1-m)}{a_n}\stackrel{d}{\rightarrow} \pi_0^{-1/\alpha}\zeta_\alpha,
\end{align*}
  where  $\{a_n\}$ is an integer-valued sequence satisfying $na_n^{-\alpha}l_2(a_n)\to\beta^{-1}(1-m)^{1+\alpha}$, and $\zeta_\alpha$ is an $\alpha$-stable random variable with characteristic function$$\psi(t)=\exp\left(- |t| ^\alpha\Gamma(1-\alpha)\cos\frac{\pi\alpha}{2} (1+\mathrm{i}\mathrm{sgn}(t)\tan\frac{\pi\alpha}{2}) \right),\quad t\in\mathbb{R}.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

