[Theo thm:near-critical-RSW of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] In the previous setup, there exist $c(m)>0$, only depending on $m$, such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}^{\textnormal{free}}_{\textnormal{FK}} \big( \textnormal{There exist an open circuit in } \mathrm{A}_{\frac{n}{2},n} \big) > c(m).
\end{equation}
A similar estimate holds for the dual model. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary lower phase transition of arXiv:2411.09614, 'Moment estimates for the stochastic heat equation on Cartan-Hadamard manifolds'] Suppose $\alpha>\frac{n-2}{4}$, $x\in M$, $R>0$ and $u_0\in L^\infty(M)$  satisfies $u_0\geq \varepsilon>0$ in some $B(x,R)$. If $u(t,x)$ solves (equation eq:PAM-mild form of the paper) starting from $u_0$, then for any $p\geq 2$, there exists $\beta_c(p)>0$ depending on $K_2$ such that $\beta>\beta_c(p)$ implies \begin{equation}
    \lim_{t\to+\infty}\frac{\ln\mathbb{E}[\abs{u(t,x)}^p]}{t}>0.
    \end{equation}
    Similarly for any fixed $\beta>0$, $\exists p_c(\beta)>0$ depending on $K_2$ such that $p>p_c$ implies (equation positive lyap exp of the paper).

[Definition of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] For $1 \leq p, \, q \leq \infty$ and $s \in \mathbb{R}$, the  Besov space with dominating mixed smoothness is defined by
\begin{equation}
 S^{s}_{p,q}B(\mathbb{R}^2)  :  = \Big\{ f \in \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^2)~:~ \,   \sum_{\bar{j} \in \mathbb{N}^2 }  2^{(j_1+j_2)sq} \Vert \Delta_{\bar{j}} f \Vert_p^q < \infty \Big\}
\end{equation}
with the norm
$$
\Vert f \Vert_{S^{s}_{p,q}B(\mathbb{R}^2)} = \left( \sum_{\bar{j} \in \mathbb{N}^2 }  2^{(j_1+j_2)sq} \Vert \Delta_{\bar{j}} f \Vert_p^q \right)^{1/q},
$$
with the usual modification if $q= \infty$.

[Lemma lem:wasserstein_bound_from_global of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] {3Ddimers}}]
       Suppose that $B\subset R$ is a connected region with piecewise smooth boundary. If $\mu,\nu$ are component measures supported in $R$ and $\mathbb{W}_1^{1,1}(\mu,\nu)<\delta$, then there is a constant $C(B)$ such that 
       \begin{align}
           \mathbb{W}_1^{1,1}(\mu\mid_{B},\nu\mid_{B}) < \delta + (C(B)+1)\delta^{1/2}.
       \end{align}
       Further, the constant $C(B)$ is bounded by the relation that $C(B)\delta^{1/2}\leq 2 \text{Vol}(\partial B, \delta^{1/2})$, the volume of the width $\delta^{1/2}$ annulus with inner boundary $\partial B$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 5 (Density of $\Xstar_T$ in a pure-jump model with a time-dependent weight (possibly vanishing)) of arXiv:2608.24294, 'Existence of densities and atoms for the running maximum of time-inhomogeneous jump diffus'] Let Assumption~\ref{ass:Levy} hold and consider
\begin{equation}
\dd X_t=b(t,X_t)\dt+\kappa(t)\,\dd L_t,\qquad X_0=x.
\end{equation}
Under Assumption~\ref{ass:jump}, for every $T>0$ the law of $\Xstar_T$ is absolutely continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure on $\R$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

