[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.03958, '2609.03958'] Let $n\geq 2$ and $K\geq 0$. Suppose that  $\kappa\in \Gamma_2$ satisfies $\kappa_1\geq\ldots \geq \kappa_n\geq -K$ and $\sigma_2(\kappa)=f$ with $f_0\leq f \leq f_1$ for two constants $f_1\geq f_0>0$.  Then there exists some constant $C>0$ depending only on $n$, $K$, $f_0$ and $f_1$ such that
\begin{equation}
\mathcal C(\kappa)\geq-C H^2.
\end{equation}

[Corollary cor:LG-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The one-point Fredholm determinant
$F_{t, a, n} = \det(I - K_{t, a, n})$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
F_{t+1, a, n+1} F_{t, a+1, n}
- q F_{t, a, n} F_{t+1, a+1, n+1}
- p F_{t+1, a+1, n} F_{t, a, n+1}
= 0,
\end{equation}
at every $(t, a, n)$ with $a < y_{n+1} - 1$.

