body:
[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2609.02175, '2609.02175'] Let $g$ be a smooth Riemannian metric on $\mathbb R^n$,
	$n\geq3$. Assume that there exists $R>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\operatorname{supp}(g-g_0)\Subset B(0,R),
	\end{equation}
	and that $(B(0,R),g)$ is simple. If
	\begin{equation}
		\|S_{g,h}(\lambda)-S_{g_0,h}(\lambda)\|
		_{\mathcal B(L^2(\mathbb S^{n-1}))}
		=
		o(1),
		\qquad h\to0,
	\end{equation}
	then there exists a diffeomorphism
	\begin{equation}
		\psi:B(0,R)\longrightarrow B(0,R),
		\qquad
		\psi|_{\partial B(0,R)}
		=
		\operatorname{Id},
	\end{equation}
	such that
	\begin{equation}
		g
		=
		\psi^*g_0.
	\end{equation}

