[Lemma 3 (Evolution of the area and its push-forward) of arXiv:2609.00501, 'Uniqueness of Finite-Time Varifold Limits for the M\"obius-Invariant Willmore Flow'] Let $X_t:=\partial_tF_t$.  Then the induced area measure on the fixed
domain satisfies
\begin{equation}

 \partial_t\dd\mu_t
 =-\langle H_t,X_t\rangle\dd\mu_t
 =a_t^{-2}\langle H_t,G_t\rangle\dd\mu_t.
\end{equation}
Moreover, for every $\varphi\in C^1(\Sph^3)$,
\begin{equation}

 \begin{aligned}
 \frac{\dd}{\dd t}\int_{\Sph^3}\varphi\dd\lambda_t
 &=\int_\Sigma
 \left[
  \big\langle\nabla^{\Sph^3}\varphi(F_t),X_t\big\rangle
  -\varphi(F_t)\langle H_t,X_t\rangle
 \right]\dd\mu_t\\
 &=\int_\Sigma a_t^{-2}
 \left[
  -\big\langle\nabla^{\Sph^3}\varphi(F_t),G_t\big\rangle
  +\varphi(F_t)\langle H_t,G_t\rangle
 \right]\dd\mu_t.
 \end{aligned}
\end{equation}

[Lemma def:irreducibility22 of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let the assumptions and conventions of the present section hold. Then, the sequence $\{Z_n\}$ is reducible in the sense of Definition (def:irreducibility of the paper) (see also Remark (r:reducible of the paper)-{\rm (redCLTconda of the paper),(redCLTcondb of the paper),(redCLTcondc of the paper)}) if and only if there exist partitions $\{B_1,\ldots,B_{m_n}\} = \{B^{(n)}_1,\ldots,B^{(n)}_{m_n}\}$ of the vertex sets $V_n$, such that, as $n \to \infty$,
    \begin{enumerate}[label={\rm (\roman*')}]
    \item  $m_n\to \infty$;
    \item  $\sum_{i=1}^{m_n} E(B_i,B_i) \sim |\mathcal{E}_n|$;
    \item  $\max_{i=1,...,m_n} E(B_i,B_i) = o\big(|\mathcal{E}_n|\big)$.  
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

