[Lemma 30 (Triangular-array Bai--Yin bound) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] Let \(Z_{ij,N}\), \(1\le i<j\le N\), be independent centered variables and
let \(W_N(i,j)=N^{-1/2}Z_{ij,N}\), \(W_N(i,i)=0\).  Suppose
\begin{align}
 \max_{i<j}\left|\E Z_{ij,N}^2-1\right|&\longrightarrow0,
 \\
 \lim_{R\to\infty}\limsup_{N\to\infty}
 \max_{i<j}
 \E\!\left[|Z_{ij,N}|^4
 \one_{\{|Z_{ij,N}|>R\}}\right]&=0.

\end{align}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \norm{W_N}_{\op}\longrightarrow2
 \qquad\text{in probability}.
\end{equation}
The conclusion remains valid uniformly over a family of triangular arrays
for which the two moduli in
\eqref{eq:R4-BY-variance}--\eqref{eq:R4-BY-tail} are uniform.

[Definition def:isoperimetric-constant of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Let $(\mathcal M,g)$ be a compact Riemannian manifold of dimension $N$ without boundary, the isoperimetric constant is defined as:
