{"artifact_digest":"sha256:098dcb2d52217e5bf47896a66951dcef4aa6172d13106c835f83224644c0e575","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/09/098dcb2d52217e5bf47896a66951dcef4aa6172d13106c835f83224644c0e575.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:19f78053a227ffa9cb29b297c6c21bf0233ea5eb54397398699a3a08ade591bf","bundle_entry_key":"2604-24914-lemma-19-lem-hypb","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_019","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_019.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2604-24914-lemma-19-lem-hypb","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: In the case of the heat equation, it is known that for any $t>0$,
\begin{equation}

K(t)=\sup_{\eta \in \mathbb{R}^d} \int_{\mathbb{R}^d} e^{-t|\xi+\eta|^2}\mu(d\xi)= \int_{\mathbb{R}^d} e^{-t|\xi|^2}\mu(d\xi),
