[Proposition AUIASLc of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] Consider the setting of Proposition~(POINT of the paper). Let \( (x_i)_{i \geq 1} \) be an arbitrary sequence in \( \mathbb{R}^d \). Then there exists an increasing sequence \( (s_n)_{n \geq 1} \) with \( s_n \to \infty \) as \( n \to \infty \), such that
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{s_n \rightarrow \infty} \mathbf{P}\left(d\left(\varphi^{s_n}_{\omega^-}(x_i), \overline{\mathcal{A}}(\omega^-)\right) \geq t \right) = 0,
	\end{align*}
	for all \( i \in \mathbb{N} \) and \( t > 0 \). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

