body:
[Prop 3 of arXiv:2609.03777, '2609.03777'] There is an isomorphism of weight-graded algebras
\begin{align}
\ha^{\geq2}_\ast\cong\hadm_\ast[z_2]\,.
\end{align}
Equivalently, every $w\in\ha^{\geq2}$ can be written uniquely as
\begin{align}
w=\sum_{j=0}^d a_j\ast z_2^{\ast j},
\qquad a_j\in\hadm\,,
\end{align}
where $z_2^{\ast0}=1$.

