[Proposition prop:central-tower of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] The truncations $\pi_N:G^{(N+1)}\to G^{(N)}$ are surjective group homomorphisms with central kernel
\begin{equation}
\ker\pi_N=\exp(\mathfrak{L}_{N+1})\cong\mathbb{R}^{\ell_d(N+1)}.
\end{equation}
Hence the representation ladder
\begin{equation}
\cdots\twoheadrightarrow\mathrm{Sig}^{(N+1)}\twoheadrightarrow\mathrm{Sig}^{(N)}\twoheadrightarrow\cdots
\end{equation}
is a tower of central extensions, each step forgetting exactly the top-degree free-Lie directions, of dimension the Witt number $\ell_d(N+1)$.

[Prop 4 of arXiv:2506.13661, 'Box-Covariances of Hyperuniform Point Processes'] Let $\eta$ be a stationary point process with truncated pair correlation measure $\beta.$ It holds that 
	\begin{align}
		\mathrm{Cov} (\eta(\Lambda_n),\eta(\Lambda_n(nz)))= \lambda_d(\Lambda_n\cap\Lambda_n(nz)) + \int_{\Lambda_n}\beta(\Lambda_n(nz-x))\lambda_d(\mathrm{d}x).
	\end{align}

