[Proposition prop:uniform-transfer-final of arXiv:2606.29557, 'Propagation of chaos for Belavkin equations beyond pure states'] For every fixed \(n\ge1\) and \(T>0\), there exists
\(C_{T,n}<\infty\), independent of \(N\) and
\(\eta\in(0,1]\), such that
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  &\sup_{0\le t\le T}
  \mathbb E_{\mathbb Q^{N,\alpha}}
  \left[
    \left\|
      \rho_t^{N:n,\alpha}
      -
      \Gamma_t^{N,\alpha,n}
    \right\|_1
  \right] \le
  \sup_{0\le t\le T}
  \mathbb E_{\mathbb Q^{N,\beta}}
  \left[
    \left\|
      \rho_t^{N:n,\beta}
      -
      \Gamma_t^{N,\beta,n}
    \right\|_1
  \right]
  +
  C_{T,n}d_N.
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}

