[Lemma 5 (anisotropic Sobolev embedding) of arXiv:2609.01093, 'Ideal MHD below the classical well-posedness threshold'] Let
\begin{equation}
 \sreg>\frac{n-1}{2},\qquad \preg\ge0,\qquad \sreg+\preg>\frac n2 .
\end{equation}
Then every $f\in Y^{\sreg,\preg}(\Rn)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \|f\|_{L^\infty(\Rn)}
 \le
 \frac{C(n,\sreg,\preg,v_{\rm A})}
 {(\sreg+\preg-\frac n2)^{1/2}}
 \|f\|_{Y^{\sreg,\preg}} .
\end{equation}
Both strict inequalities in \eqref{eq:Y-embed-range} are necessary.

[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2604.16795, '2604.16795'] Under Assumption {\rm\ref{A0}}, for any measurable function $\phi$ on $\R^d$ satisfying
	\begin{align}
		\int_{\R^d} H_{c,c_0}(y) |\phi(y)| \,\mu(\d y) <\infty
	\end{align} with $c>0$ large enough and $c_0>0$ small enough,
	there are constants $T_0>0$ and $C_0>0$ such that all $t > T_0$,
	\begin{align}
		\|e^{\lambda_0t}P_t(\phi)-\Pi(\phi)\|_{L^{\infty}(\mu)}
		\le C_0 e^{-(\lambda_1-\lambda_0)t}.
	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] We consider the setting of Theorem~(thm_main_R of the paper) and $\mathcal H_t $ be the event $\{\tau^{X}_0<t\} = \{\exists\; s \in [0,t) \colon  X_s = 0\}$.
The statistic 
\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned}
		\varrho_n(X) &= \left(4  \sqrt{\frac 2 \pi} \right) \frac{1}{\sqrt n}\frac{\cD{2}{n,\cdot}(X)}{ \cD{1}{n,\cdot}(X)}
	\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
is a consistent estimators of $\rho $, conditionally on the event $\mathcal H_t $, i.e., $\varrho_n(X)  \longrightarrow  \rho $, in $\Prob^{\mathcal H_t}_x $-probability, as $n \longrightarrow  \infty $.

