[Definition def:APZ of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] A line ensemble $\mathbf{X}$ is asymptotically pinned to zero if for any $ \varepsilon, T > 0$ there is some
$k \in \mathbb{N}$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[ \sup_{t \in [-T,T]} X^k(t) \leqslant \varepsilon \mright] \geqslant 1 - \varepsilon.
\end{equation}

