body:
[Proposition 5 (Reduced-form PX-EM loading objective) of arXiv:2608.21551, '\bf Sparse Separable Factor Analysis in the Complex Domain with an Application to Local Fi'] After updating $\Gammab$ according to \eqref{eq:app_gamma_update} and applying the parameter-reduction map in  \eqref{eq:lam_construction}, the loading-dependent part of the normalized PX-EM objective in \eqref{eq:vec-comp-llk_app} satisfies
\begin{align}

  \frac{1}{n}
  \Qcal\left(
    \tilde{\Lambdab},
    \Gammab^{(t+1)},
    \Psib^{(t)}
    \mid
    \tilde{\thetab}^{(t)}
  \right)
  \doteq \Qcal_{\Lambdab}^{\mathrm{red}}
  \left(
    \Lambdab
    \mid
    \thetab^{(t)}
  \right) =
  \tr\left[
    \left(
      \Lambdab-\Ab^{(t)}
    \right)^\star
    \left(\Psib^{(t)}\right)^{-1}
    \left(
      \Lambdab-\Ab^{(t)}
    \right)
  \right],
\end{align}
where $\Lambdab = \tilde{\Lambdab} \operatorname{chol}\left(\Gammab^{(t+1)} \right)$, $\Ab^{(t)}$ is defined in \eqref{eq:lam_quadratic_form_final_app}, and $\doteq$ denotes equality up to an additive term that does not depend on $\Lambdab$. The unique unpenalized minimizer of the objective in  \eqref{eq:lam_quadratic_form_final_app} is $\Lambdab^{(t+1)} = \Ab^{(t)}$.

