[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2608.27500, 'Optimal Transport for Network Comparison: \\ A Review with Machine Learning Applications'] Let $G'=(V,E')$ be a subgraph of $G=(V,E)$, with $|V|=n$, and $|E'|=|E|-1$. If $\mu_G=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n \delta_{\lambda_i}$ and $\mu_{G'}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n \delta_{\lambda_i'}$, then
    \begin{align*}
        W_1(\mu_G,\mu_{G'})=\frac{2}{n}.
    \end{align*}

