[Lemma l:error_uniform_bound of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $Q$ be a parabolic cylinder with side length $\varrho\in (0,1/2]$ and center $(t_0,x_0)\in {\mathbb R}_+\times {\mathbb R}^d$.
For all $r\in (1,\infty)$, there exists a constant $C>0$ depending only on $\mu,r,\varrho$ and $d$ such that, for all $N\geq 1$, $\delta\in (0,1]$ and any local solution $(v^{N,\delta},\pi^{N,\delta},(\widetilde{\pi}^{N,\delta}_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha})$ to (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_quantitative of the paper), it holds that 
\begin{align*}
\big({\mathbf E} \|\mathrm{Err}^{{\rm det}}\|_{L^2(I;H^{-1}(B))}^r \big)^{1/r}
+ \big({\mathbf E}\|(\mathrm{Err}^{{\rm sto}}_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha}\|_{L^2(Q;\ell^2)}^r\big)^{1/r}
\leq C  
\big({\mathbf E}\|G\|_{L^2(Q)}^r\big)^{1/r}\qquad &\\+
C\big({\mathbf E}\|\nabla v^{N,\delta}\|_{L^2(Q)}^r \big)^{1/r}
+C\big({\mathbf E} \|(\nabla \widetilde{\pi}_{k,\alpha}^{N,\delta})_{k,\alpha}\|_{L^2(Q;\ell^2)}^r\big)^{1/r}.&
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 29 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Cumulative Distribution Functions}


    Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $\R^n$ and $X \sim \nu$. Respectively, define the empirical and average marginal cumulative distribution functions at $x \in \R$ as 
    \begin{align*}
        \hat F_n(x)
        := \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n \indicator{X_i \leq x}, 
        \quad \text{and} \quad 
        \bar F(x)
        := \E[\hat F_n(x)]
        = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n \P(X_i \leq x). 
    \end{align*}

