[Definition 12 (Super-regular pair) of arXiv:2604.05138, 'Convergence rate of $H$-property for step-graphons'] Let $G$ be an undirected graph, and $A,B$ be two disjoint subsets of $V(G)$.
The pair $(A,B)$ is {\bf $(\epsilon,\delta)$-super-regular} if
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
e(X,Y) &> \delta |X||Y|, 
\\
&\text{for any } X \subseteq A,\; Y \subseteq B
\\
&\text{with } |X| > \epsilon |A|,\; |Y| > \epsilon |B|,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and, moreover,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
e(a,B) &> \delta |B|, && \mbox{for all } a \in A, \\
e(b,A) &> \delta |A|, && \mbox{for all } b \in B.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

